{"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/endlength"]}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"endLength","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLEndingV9endLengthSdSgvp","role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"endLength","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTenths","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"property"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"endLength","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTenths","kind":"typeIdentifier","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Maps to the MusicXML ","type":"text"},{"code":"end-length","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" attribute.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"The length of the downward jog at the end of the ending line.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/endLength","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTenths":{"title":"MXLTenths","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"typealias","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLTenths","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltenths","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTenths","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLTenths","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The tenths type is a number representing tenths of interline staff space (positive or negative). Both integer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and decimal values are allowed, such as 5 for a half space and 2.5 for a quarter space. Interline space is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured from the middle of a staff line."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLEnding","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLEnding","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The ending type represents multiple (e.g. first and second) endings. Typically, the start type is associated"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the left barline of the first measure in an ending. The stop and discontinue types are associated with"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the right barline of the last measure in an ending. Stop is used when the ending mark concludes with a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"downward jog, as is typical for first endings. Discontinue is used when there is no downward jog, as is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"typical for second endings that do not conclude a piece. The length of the jog can be specified using the end-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length attribute. The text-x and text-y attributes are offsets that specify where the baseline of the start of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the ending text appears, relative to the start of the ending line."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending","title":"MXLEnding"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","role":"collection","title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLEnding/endLength":{"title":"endLength","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"endLength"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL9MXLTenthsa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLTenths"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The length of the downward jog at the end of the ending line.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlending\/endlength","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLEnding\/endLength"}}}